33:Run the prototype with `uv run python -m mgraph.map_server` and open `http://127.0.0.1:8765`. The Proximity map loads connected group summaries eight at a time as the horizontal canvas scrolls; it never plots standalone entries. Each visible group loads 24 new entries per page, with bridge entries from earlier pages so every displayed entry remains connected. Offscreen group cards and edges are discarded. Persisted pair scores drive spring distances, pair feedback overrides model scores, and closer-than feedback adjusts positions when all three entries are on the same page. The grouping threshold is 0.65. Group topology is cached for 30 seconds, so newly judged pairs may take up to 30 seconds to appear. Search still covers every projected entry, including entries without a profile or graph position.
35:The Library tab pages authoritative DynamoDB source records by `node`, `file`, `link`, `collection`, `property`, and `linkTag`. On `node`, the `Profiled entries only` filter limits search, counts, and pagination to source records with a saved profile. Record details show raw source fields, associated root entry evidence, extraction output, profile concepts/tags/properties/claims, and embedding and pair-judgment status when available. The entry API also returns each extraction's identity status and reason; the Library continues to expose raw quarantined text for inspection, while MCP reads omit it. The library reads hosted PostgreSQL and does not download R2 snapshots or rerun inference. For a manual check, open the library, filter to profiled entries, search and advance a filtered page, inspect a profile, switch resources, then return to the map and open a connected node. The map is a pilot visualization, and group coordinates are recalculated within each displayed page rather than being stable global coordinates.

